<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 84 0 R
/T (Business Question Answer Recommend inventory adjustments for underperforming and high-demand products. ToyJoy should reduce stock for slow-moving products in Puzzles and Dolls, especially products with high stock and low revenue. At the same time, high-demand products such as Math Learning Kit, STEM Kit, Coding Toy, and Superhero Figure should be stocked more aggressively. This will reduce blocked inventory while improving product availability for strong sellers.)
/E (Business Question Answer Recommend inventory adjustments for underperforming and high-demand products. ToyJoy should reduce stock for slow-moving products in Puzzles and Dolls, especially products with high stock and low revenue. At the same time, high-demand products such as Math Learning Kit, STEM Kit, Coding Toy, and Superhero Figure should be stocked more aggressively. This will reduce blocked inventory while improving product availability for strong sellers.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 84 0 R
/T (Business Question Answer Suggest strategies to optimize reorder points and quantities to reduce overstock and stockouts. Reorder points should be increased for high-demand products, especially Educational Toys and top Action Figures. For slow-moving products, reorder quantities should be reduced and replenishment should happen less frequently. Seasonal demand should also be considered while planning stock for festivals, holidays, and Back-to-School periods. This will help ToyJoy maintain a better inventory balance.)
/E (Business Question Answer Suggest strategies to optimize reorder points and quantities to reduce overstock and stockouts. Reorder points should be increased for high-demand products, especially Educational Toys and top Action Figures. For slow-moving products, reorder quantities should be reduced and replenishment should happen less frequently. Seasonal demand should also be considered while planning stock for festivals, holidays, and Back-to-School periods. This will help ToyJoy maintain a better inventory balance.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
